From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add DS video

display_nds.c replaces the SDL driver: BUILD renders the 256x192 top
screen at its own resolution, scaling the menus and HUD as it does at any
resolution, into main RAM, and DMA copies each frame into one of two 8bpp
VRAM pages a few rows at a time, chained by interrupts, while the game
goes on. Pages and palette are flipped on vblank, a palette set on a still
screen, such as the end of a fade, is shown on its own. The 120 Hz timer
counts from the hardware tick counter, the buttons come as keyboard
scancodes. Banks C, D and E hold tables that are only read once made.
